# Rings that move outward, like a stone dropped in still water, in three colours.
#   ./intent svg examples/art/rings.intent --after "wait 300" --style blocks
# The distance from the middle picks the ring; the ring picks the colour.

The board is 41 wide and 41 high.
Cells have an x (number), a y (number), a ring (number), a look (text) and a hue (text).
At the start there is a cell for every x from 1 to 41 and every y from 1 to 41, whose ring is 0, whose look is " " and whose hue is "red".
The tick starts at 0.

Every 100 milliseconds, the tick increases by 1.
Every 100 milliseconds, set the ring of each cell to the square root of ((its x minus 21) times (its x minus 21) plus (its y minus 21) times (its y minus 21)) minus the tick.
Every 100 milliseconds, set the look of each cell to "#" if (its ring plus 300) modulo 3 is 0, otherwise " ".
Every 100 milliseconds, set the hue of each cell to "red" if (its ring plus 300) modulo 9 is 0, otherwise "yellow" if (its ring plus 300) modulo 9 is 3, otherwise "magenta".

Draw each cell as its look in its hue at its x and its y.
